{"case_id":"T8018","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry point","API protocol","input semantics"],"commit_induced":"YES","maintenance_needed":true,"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["xmlNodeSetLang","xmlNodeSetSpacePreserve","xmlSetProp"],"reason":"S1 materially changes three public entry points that H0 cannot invoke. xmlNodeSetLang and xmlNodeSetSpacePreserve change from void to int, introduce observable 0/1/-1 result protocols, and change accepted-input behavior; xmlNodeSetSpacePreserve now maps every nonzero val to \"preserve\". xmlSetProp changes QName parsing through xmlSplitQName4 and namespace lookup behavior. H0 declares OP_XML_NODE_SET_LANG and OP_XML_NODE_SET_SPACE_PRESERVE but implements no switch cases for them, while its only OP_XML_SET_PROP case is disabled by #if 0. Thus S1 adds materially changed behavior and API outcomes to already-unreached entry points, aggravating the gap. The changed getters xmlNodeGetLang and xmlNodeGetSpacePreserve remain directly reachable and controllable through their existing opcodes, so they do not independently require maintenance.","evidence":["H0's opType contains OP_XML_NODE_SET_LANG and OP_XML_NODE_SET_SPACE_PRESERVE with /* TODO */, but LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput has no corresponding case labels.","The only case OP_XML_SET_PROP in H0 is enclosed in #if 0, so xmlSetProp is not called by the harness.","include/libxml/tree.h changes xmlNodeSetLang and xmlNodeSetSpacePreserve return types from void to int.","S1 xmlNodeSetLang returns 1 for NULL or non-XML_ELEMENT_NODE inputs, propagates xmlSearchNsByHrefSafe results, and returns -1 when xmlSetNsProp returns NULL.","S1 xmlNodeSetSpacePreserve introduces the same result protocol and changes value handling from cases 0 and 1 only to val == 0 versus every other value.","S1 xmlSetProp replaces xmlSplitQName3/xmlStrndup processing with xmlSplitQName4 and an explicit localname/prefix protocol.","H0 directly invokes xmlNodeGetLang under OP_XML_NODE_GET_LANG and xmlNodeGetSpacePreserve under OP_XML_NODE_GET_SPACE_PRESERVE using register-controlled nodes."],"recommended_action":"Implement the existing OP_XML_NODE_SET_LANG and OP_XML_NODE_SET_SPACE_PRESERVE cases and enable or replace OP_XML_SET_PROP. Feed register-controlled nodes, strings, and arbitrary integer val values; capture the new integer results and apply OOM reporting for negative returns."}
